<!--
  The hand-maintained half of the sitemap: pages that exist because we wrote
  them, not because a row exists. Everything data-driven (works, authors,
  publishers — 1,227 URLs and growing) is generated by the API and served at
  /sitemaps/index.xml. Both are declared in robots.txt.

  Two rules this file has to keep.

  1. LIST FINAL URLS, NEVER REDIRECTS. It used to list /privacy.html and
     /terms.html; Cloudflare Pages 308s those to the extensionless form, so
     every crawl produced a "Page with redirect" in Search Console — the
     sitemap pointing at the wrong URL for the two pages the app stores
     require to be reachable.

  2. ONLY INDEXABLE PAGES. /browse and /search are noindex by design (faceted
     browse explodes combinatorially), so listing them would ask Google to
     index pages that tell it not to. The genre hubs were once omitted
     under the same rule for a different reason — not one work carried a
     genre, so they were real pages over an empty set. That stopped being true
     when the W5 classification landed; they are listed below.

  lastmod is when the page's content last changed, not when this file was
  edited — a sitemap claiming everything changed today teaches crawlers to
  ignore the field.
-->
